body:
**Do you want to request a *feature* or report a *bug*?**

A bug

**Bug: What is the current behavior?**

I use the example code from the documentation: https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/documentation/#hide-results-on-init

```js
var search = instantsearch({
  [...],
  searchFunction: function(helper) {
    var searchResults = $('.search-results');
    if (helper.state.query === '') {
      searchResults.hide();
      return;
    }
    helper.search();
    searchResults.show();
  }
}
```

Here is a JSFiddle: https://jsfiddle.net/4jqgawpk/3/

Open the HTML iframe: https://fiddle.jshell.net/4jqgawpk/3/show/ (please try in Firefox, somehow the URL is not updated in Chrome, probably because of JSFiddle)

Type a search, wait for the URL params to update

Empty the search box

The URL params are not reset, the last search query is still there.

**Bug: What is the expected behavior?**

When I empty the search box, I expect the URL to be "clean" (at least the `q` param should be empty).

**Bug: What browsers are impacted? Which versions?**

Firefox latest, Chrome latest

**Bug: What is the proposed solution?**

There should probably be a way to use the JS helper to reset the URL params. If possible, the example from the documentation should be updated to use it.
